  "entities": [
    {
      "entityId": "fact.caldris.era.the-long-reprieve-and-fraying-peace",
      "name": "Era — The Long Reprieve and Fraying Peace",
      "components": [
        {
          "qualifiedTypeId": "game.core.world.fact",
          "value": {
            "status": "active",
            "summary": "560 AS to present. The Three Banner War ended in 560 AS after six years of confused alliances, failed sieges, disease, and one winter in which soldiers on both sides informally stopped fighting to repair the same flood bank. The Lantern Sea Accord established protected grain routes, prisoner exchange, pilgrim rights, and regular diplomatic congresses. Eighty-three years later, the generation that remembers the war is fading. New officials treat peace as an administrative fact rather than a hard-won habit. Recent events include the Summer Without Swallows, the death of two heirs in unrelated accidents, counterfeit seven-sided seals, unusual dragon signs, and a rise in “temporary” tolls that never expire. ## The twelve polities | Continent | Polity | Form | Capital | Other primary cities | Present pressure | | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | | Eredane | Alderwick | Kingdom | Merecross | Highmead, Dunwarren | A childless queen, aggressive toll reform, and a suspiciously organize…",
            "provenance": "Caldris world bible — seven eras",
            "visibility": "public"
          }
        },
        {
          "qualifiedTypeId": "game.core.world.knowledge.classification",
          "value": {
            "subjectKind": "event",
            "sensitivity": "open"
          }
        }
      ],
      "containment": {
        "containerEntityId": "location.caldris.atlas",
        "slot": "knowledge"
      }
    },
    {
      "entityId": "fact.caldris.era.the-river-thrones",
      "name": "Era — The River Thrones",
      "components": [
        {
          "qualifiedTypeId": "game.core.world.fact",
          "value": {
            "status": "active",
            "summary": "c. 1900–840 BS. Irrigation, bronze and early iron, walled river towns, written toll records, and dynastic temples produced the first durable states. Eredane's lower Mere and Solasca's Aur and Namar valleys grew powerful independently, then discovered one another through sea trade. Present residues: canal alignments, royal burial islands, inherited water courts, archaic weights, and several city districts built above older streets. The period ended through regional collapses, not one universal disaster.",
            "provenance": "Caldris world bible — seven eras",
            "visibility": "public"
          }
        },
        {
          "qualifiedTypeId": "game.core.world.knowledge.classification",
          "value": {
            "subjectKind": "event",
            "sensitivity": "open"
          }
        }
      ],
      "containment": {
        "containerEntityId": "location.caldris.atlas",
        "slot": "knowledge"
      }
    },
    {
      "entityId": "fact.caldris.era.the-sundering-of-seals",
      "name": "Era — The Sundering of Seals",
      "components": [
        {
          "qualifiedTypeId": "game.core.world.fact",
          "value": {
            "status": "active",
            "summary": "116 BS–1 AS. The Concord collapsed over a century. Grain failures, forged tallies, regional revolts, unpaid escorts, dragon interference, succession struggles, and competing reforms all contributed. The last High Assessor disappeared during negotiations at Aster Quay. In Year 1 AS, twelve successor delegations publicly broke the master seal and declared old hereditary debts void. Present residues: abandoned archive forts, disputed land, missing ledgers, noble families founded by rebels and auditors alike, and a deep fear of centralized record power. The secret Seventh Ledger society believes the Concord fell because it compromised, not because it controlled too much.",
            "provenance": "Caldris world bible — seven eras",
            "visibility": "public"
          }
        },
        {
          "qualifiedTypeId": "game.core.world.knowledge.classification",
          "value": {
            "subjectKind": "event",
            "sensitivity": "open"
          }
        }
      ],
      "containment": {
        "containerEntityId": "location.caldris.atlas",
        "slot": "knowledge"
      }
    },
